matrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $4$th column). \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A))=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319325 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b6e6369-f36d-5623-9707-d061079c4b16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317608} {:answer/id #uuid "6e16f265-439b-518c-bffe-6ada0c73863b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317947} {:answer/id #uuid "83764eea-1cac-51e6-b6ee-b9b6ddf31787" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318008} {:answer/id #uuid "c425a5ec-2aee-5332-8b9e-bbed46cc213f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318214} {:answer/id #uuid "d6bf57b2-15fe-53c3-ab3e-8e10ccff6b38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318278}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317947} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a79897d-fbc5-5115-bc78-31d1bd2e07ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318681}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "73aa3ed9-e9f3-503a-8a62-188955d58a4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-34914" :question/problem "Given $$\n\\displaystyle Q=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 12 & 7 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 16 & 8 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -12 & -3 & -10\\end{bmatrix},\\,\n$$ what is $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(Q))?$" :question/worked-solution "To find $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(Q))$, we reduce $Q$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 12 & 7 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 16 & 8 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -12 & -3 & -10\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 16 & 8 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -12 & -3 & -10\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -12 & -3 & -10\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{5} & :={R}_{5}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $5$ pivot columns and no non-pivot columns. \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(Q))=0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319342 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0aae1275-e9c6-5b69-b2d2-7024fc406552" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317605} {:answer/id #uuid "17e6da27-ee73-5c8e-a176-7f8b283f0fcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317640} {:answer/id #uuid "21ff139f-6473-5484-9776-a027b6b32971" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317670} {:answer/id #uuid "4fe85fb9-4a34-558d-a85e-6ac172770001" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317828} {:answer/id #uuid "b2c25cb4-3f94-556b-8283-c725a3b9e219" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318170}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186318170} :answer-field/id #uuid "042814c9-6b45-5d98-b930-dabadf8ec776" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318434}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ade7d6b0-58df-5513-bc22-de237a49cc42" :question/math-academy-id "q-34947" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$ and the vector $b=\\begin{bmatrix}k \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find the value of $k$ such that $b\\in \\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "If $b\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then we must have $Ab=0.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}k \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}-2k-8 \\\\ k+4\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2k-8 &=0 \\\\ k+4 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=-4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319352 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e278eb04-9ea2-5844-b05e-b7780ac79ae8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450554} {:answer/id #uuid "9c39f12c-2213-5317-b25b-2b94303ac001" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450555}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186450555} :answer-field/id #uuid "2574fec4-c774-5e83-88c2-54c6e3934238" :answer-field/key "If $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451231} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e20627b5-0399-56be-bf11-b108f477de32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450556} {:answer/id #uuid "fd76fc07-6256-5abb-ada4-e6122e1a413e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450557}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186450556} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4b81185-37e8-5204-a76c-9cca612b39b1" :answer-field/key "If $B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(B))=3.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451232} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b008e94-bd7d-587f-b70b-14f6d36a4468" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450558} {:answer/id #uuid "f5a6b4d9-1c23-50e1-93df-86fd6c5da0a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450559}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186450558} :answer-field/id #uuid "9da1ea97-6d5c-56ad-aad8-3bac4d1c60b6" :answer-field/key "If $C=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(C))=2.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451233}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "56ebc46d-299b-5fda-a402-a93bacc04806" :question/math-academy-id "q-34973" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- Statement “If $$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2.$” is true. The matrix $A$ has $3$ pivot columns and $2$ non-pivot columns. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2.\n$$\n\n- Statement “If $B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(B))=3.$” is false. The matrix $B$ has $3$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $4$th column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement “If $C=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(C))=2.$” is false. The matrix $C$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $2$nd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(C))=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “If $$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2.$” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321072 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3481e207-e3b3-5e18-a809-b68d786d6e91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319553} {:answer/id #uuid "49662fce-308a-5973-9daf-90f661164bb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319609} {:answer/id #uuid "85f18eb3-e6ce-502e-be45-f3e00050dbb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319794} {:answer/id #uuid "b176021e-5d4f-5d30-bf8d-ae821e8d1a70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319934} {:answer/id #uuid "ca6939af-8bae-5b13-92b7-db8af3689ee5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320010}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319609} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c4879d1-521b-5d88-bd53-72f2ed650b99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320450}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "da3efbc4-2fa4-54a8-9aa9-e1c2c723490a" :question/math-academy-id "q-35316" :question/problem "Consider the matrices given below. Find $\\,\\text{dim(Null}(A))+\\text{dim(Null}(B))+\\text{dim(Null}(C)).$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has $3$ pivot columns and no non-pivot column. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has $1$ pivot column and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $2$nd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=1.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has $3$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $4$th column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(C))=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))+\\text{dim(Null}(B))+\\text{dim(Null}(C))=0+1+1=2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321074 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51f92107-6ac3-540e-a6af-eba636094019" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319628} {:answer/id #uuid "5b14edc3-6282-5d3c-935a-14f212120710" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319661} {:answer/id #uuid "68f6d7f2-9041-5fcd-ab33-220d0a2e3212" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319714} {:answer/id #uuid "aff2d8bb-74ce-5205-bed5-5f76fc9e9b08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319925} {:answer/id #uuid "f182b151-8417-5810-afe5-721f86ed67db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320113}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320113} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9ee2a36-88e1-57f0-a43d-4439f08f9550" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320506}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5c9fb6cf-01de-5080-82f7-0128ba4fbceb" :question/math-academy-id "q-35317" :question/problem "If $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 3 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 4 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,$ then $\\text{nullity}(A)=$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that by definition, $\\text{nullity}(A)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A)).$\n\nTo find $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A))$, we reduce $A$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 3 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 4 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 3 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 9 & 28\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-7){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 3 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 23 & 56\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot columns. \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(A)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A))=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321076 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15f82c38-57d7-5235-83eb-302196ff1750" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319454} {:answer/id #uuid "3f67abcd-6c02-50c4-acb1-27ca9fadc6b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319583} {:answer/id #uuid "49c006d4-4694-5f18-8c18-fd8cb1aef987" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319610} {:answer/id #uuid "4a702616-0a66-569b-9818-fc0d52dc4b39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319613} {:answer/id #uuid "c8259aac-72ac-5cc7-a879-c8c2f0167118" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320001}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320001} :answer-field/id #uuid "694b1ea3-a3d2-5e40-bfa3-982b01e9a940" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320383}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "687cbaa7-684a-507a-80f4-6f515d95364b" :question/math-academy-id "q-35318" :question/problem "If $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 6 & -3 & 9\\end{bmatrix},\\,$ then $\\text{nullity}(A)=$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that by definition, $\\text{nullity}(A)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A)).$\n\nTo find $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A))$, we reduce $A$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 6 & -3 & 9\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 13 \\\\ 6 & -3 & 9\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns and no non-pivot columns. \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(A)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A))=0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321134 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04b62aea-e3f4-523f-a902-d1a9e4779b94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319406} {:answer/id #uuid "7735440e-e7f0-5b70-a465-136a465a1efe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319749} {:answer/id #uuid "a7d17f6e-8b29-519d-8ae5-8066c3d20ae8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319892} {:answer/id #uuid "c189cbe0-0365-5aef-b868-68145c4dfacf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319985} {:answer/id #uuid "ecac3b29-1726-5db0-9775-040e9c14b3da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320099}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319406} :answer-field/id #uuid "abd222bd-6da0-5c4b-b26f-2a42968d72ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320510}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a52db54f-ed58-568b-ad92-d2a1074b04ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-35348" :question/problem "Given $$\n\\displaystyle Z=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 12 & 3 & -6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 & -7 & 11 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 4 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 7 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 8 & 2 & -4 & 6\\end{bmatrix},\\,\n$$ what is $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(Z))?$" :question/worked-solution "To find $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(Z))$, we reduce $Z$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Z & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 12 & 3 & -6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 & -7 & 11 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 4 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 7 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 8 & 2 & -4 & 6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\left(-\\frac{1}{3}\\right){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 12 & 3 & -6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 & -7 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 7 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 8 & 2 & -4 & 6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{5} & :={R}_{5}+\\left(-\\frac{2}{3}\\right){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 12 & 3 & -6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 & -7 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 12 & 3 & -6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 & -7 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $4$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $4$th column). \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(Z))=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323674 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ccb0567-0495-5c74-8699-bab086a64809" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450560} {:answer/id #uuid "62954330-fa79-5088-bd4b-cb797b88fe25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450561}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186450560} :answer-field/id #uuid "c34e741f-afd5-539e-89ed-87f3b75f5ff9" :answer-field/key "$\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451234} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46523043-bc55-5cb6-b33f-a37a5b648d6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450562} {:answer/id #uuid "2d38beb7-b0db-523b-99bb-2bb27ec73198" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450563}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186450562} :answer-field/id #uuid "d46ab9df-f1e2-5ca8-bca4-a8a7559c9764" :answer-field/key "$A$ is invertible" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451235} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd58a89b-6f9b-54a1-881b-e354c7de0b9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450564} {:answer/id #uuid "2d103fe3-6dbf-53c9-a8ce-da05a06b3a9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450565}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186450565} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f8121ca-3a46-557f-84a4-3de651e3583d" :answer-field/key "$\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 5$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451236}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9288acd6-ddf2-55d8-ba92-e1c27cfdfe7c" :question/math-academy-id "q-35425" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $v=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}$  is a solution of the equation $Ax=0?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$\nA\\text{ is }\\text{invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\mathbb{R}^{5} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=5=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0$ is false. Since $v\\ne 0$ and $Av=0,$ \nthen $v\\in \\text{Null}(A)$ and, therefore, $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0.$\n\n- Statement “$A$ is invertible” is false. Since $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 5$ is true. Since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 5.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 5$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323706 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d968245-3c49-554a-a558-3152bc84519d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A2}$, $\\text{A7}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321628} {:answer/id #uuid "54949060-9a73-5ed7-81e3-57e02bbe63c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A7}$, $\\text{A3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321812} {:answer/id #uuid "7e962385-680a-55ba-bd82-e8c91d68d61f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A1}$, $\\text{A2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322143} {:answer/id #uuid "be54f2fc-40de-5124-af45-ae9b464ad500" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A4}$, $\\text{A4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322626} {:answer/id #uuid "e39549d6-eae6-57e1-9c8e-c8e25c065159" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A4}$, $\\text{A3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322928}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186322928} :answer-field/id #uuid "9aa570ad-0371-55b5-8f7a-881567300397" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323468}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9e0aac55-7230-5b2a-970b-243dc9e706c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-35661" :question/problem "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement:* \n\n*If $w$ is a vector such that $w+w=w$, then $w=0$* \n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w+w & =w &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (w+w)+(-w) & =w+(-w) &  & [\\,\\text{add }(-w)\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ w+(w+(-w)) & =w+(-w) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A2}\\,] \\\\ w+0 & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ w & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the vector space axioms, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w+w & =w &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (w+w)+(-w) & =w+(-w) &  & [\\,\\text{add }(-w)\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ w+(w+(-w)) & =w+(-w) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A2}\\,] \\\\ w+0 & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A4}\\,] \\\\ w & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326761 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "436169ad-a07f-5c25-ac9d-4c0589b9f1c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467452} {:answer/id #uuid "71172c6d-69cb-5654-9de1-529b9f219d9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467453}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467453} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcd336a4-e888-5530-80a4-1f13ce8d051e" :answer-field/key "$U={\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468447} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7391a0f0-11c6-5e13-b5fa-5c4a81d4a16c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467454} {:answer/id #uuid "c2f48a37-f6d7-54a2-8786-46b1ef3f35b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467455}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467454} :answer-field/id #uuid "32c892b1-1456-54d9-b9da-a3b642d33cca" :answer-field/key "$V={\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468448} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fe9da6f9-ff11-5873-b211-7ef3a4f05b3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467456} {:answer/id #uuid "c944e341-be44-513f-b567-efd54efb1959" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467457}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467456} :answer-field/id #uuid "6fd43aef-1a51-5e8e-bc1a-09365ae0a928" :answer-field/key "$W={\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468449}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "33270b70-b678-53b1-8691-4ebd546544ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-39396" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are orthogonal?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of the given sets as \n${{u}_{1},{u}_{2},{u}_{3}},$\n${{v}_{1},{v}_{2}},$ and \n${{w}_{1},{w}_{2},{w}_{3}},$ respectively. \n\nThe sets $U,V,$ and $W$ are orthogonal if the following conditions on each set hold:\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle {u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0,\\,{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{3}=0,\\,{u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{3}=0.\n$$\n\n- ${v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2}=0.$\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle {w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2}=0,\\,{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{3}=0,\\,{w}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{3}=0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- For the set $U,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=6-16+10=0 & ✓ \\\\ {u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{3} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=0+0+0=0 & ✓ \\\\ {u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{3} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=0+0+0=0 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the set $U$ is orthogonal.\n\n- For the set $V,$ notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=-8+10=2\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $V$ is not an orthogonal set.\n\n- For the set $W,$ notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=15-12-1=2\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $W$ is not an orthogonal set.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"$U$ only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326826 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06cbe622-46bf-53aa-9553-b561bf153dd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324035} {:answer/id #uuid "5514fc0c-2492-503a-a79c-cab26e0e75a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324679} {:answer/id #uuid "5c9d808e-70dc-571a-bfe8-07f1c66ccc3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324743} {:answer/id #uuid "84742ab7-2657-53a9-b07d-08f0840784d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325086} {:answer/id #uuid "cc50deec-6373-5c8d-871d-41bd499da9ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325743}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186324035} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c3b572b-bb9d-5b7f-a832-4603686f4018" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326471}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fc6f0331-fd7b-569e-96d9-598f3de3cd4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-40299" :question/problem "Consider the orthogonal set $U$ below. By adding a new vector $x=[{x}_{1},\\,{x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3},\\,{x}_{4}]^{T},$ extend the set so that it forms an orthogonal basis of ${R}^{4}.$ What is the value of $\\frac{{x}_{1}}{{x}_{4}}?$\n\n$$\nU={\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $U$ as ${u}_{1},\\,{u}_{2},\\,{u}_{3}.$ To extend the given set to an orthogonal basis of ${R}^{4}$, we need to find a fourth vector $x$ such that\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot x &=0 \\\\ {u}_{2}\\cdot x &=0 \\\\ {u}_{3}\\cdot x &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}-{x}_{4} &=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}+4{x}_{4} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system above and reduce it to its row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 3 & 4 & 0\\end{array}\\right] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 6 & 4 & 0\\end{array}\\right] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 10 & 2 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are three pivot columns ($1$st, $2$nd and $3$rd). Thus, ${x}_{4}$ is a free variable. From the third and first equation, we get ${x}_{3}=-\\frac{1}{5}{x}_{4}$ and ${x}_{1}={x}_{3}=-\\frac{1}{5}{x}_{4}$, respectively. Substituting this into the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2}+2(-\\frac{1}{5}{x}_{4})-{x}_{4}=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-\\frac{7}{5}{x}_{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{5}{x}_{4} \\\\ -\\frac{7}{5}{x}_{4} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{5}{x}_{4} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{4}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{4}=5$, we obtain the vector \n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, an orthogonal basis of ${R}^{4}$ is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, $\\,\\frac{{x}_{1}}{{x}_{4}}=-\\frac{1}{5}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326836 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f0a06d8-2d1a-56c8-be6c-0de612626107" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{35}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324346} {:answer/id #uuid "6c6d60ca-7ba6-582b-8ba8-aa6a2bb6f45a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{37}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324870} {:answer/id #uuid "86278f77-2ac1-53b5-bab8-a9ea417f8fd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{35}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325108} {:answer/id #uuid "d75de039-1846-5a30-9cbb-9b88d55e855c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325843} {:answer/id #uuid "f8d2beef-eaea-5c96-adf4-c346ba078cbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326162}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186324870} :answer-field/id #uuid "108e1ca7-51ee-54a2-986d-908f36b9ba57" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326251}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7f73dfde-d126-5b7a-9d31-4cf2267cf6ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-40399" :question/problem "Consider the orthogonal set $U$ below. By adding a new vector $x=[{x}_{1},\\,{x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3}]^{T},$ extend the set so that it forms an orthogonal basis of ${R}^{3}.$ What is the value of $\\frac{{x}_{1}}{{x}_{2}}?$\n\n$$\nU={\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $U$ as ${u}_{1},\\,{u}_{2}.$ To extend the given set to an orthogonal basis of ${R}^{3}$, we need to find a third vector $x=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}$ such that\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot x &=0 \\\\ {u}_{2}\\cdot x &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}6{x}_{1}+{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-6{x}_{3} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system above and reduce it to its row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}6 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -6 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+\\left(-\\frac{1}{6}\\right){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}6 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -\\frac{37}{6} & 0\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are two pivot columns ($1$st and $2$nd). Thus, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-\\frac{37}{6}{x}_{3}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}_{1}+{x}_{3}=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-\\frac{1}{6}{x}_{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{6}{x}_{3} \\\\ -\\frac{37}{6}{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{3}=6$, we obtain the vector \n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -37 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, an orthogonal basis of ${R}^{3}$ is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -37 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, $\\frac{{x}_{1}}{{x}_{2}}=\\frac{1}{37}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329820 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86d1fafe-67a4-5304-b42b-0fa34a95eaff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467578} {:answer/id #uuid "c76c9ea4-d5d0-5c09-adc5-db52b1568fa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467579}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467579} :answer-field/id #uuid "3df948ff-c1ab-538f-b99e-ed07682677fc" :answer-field/key "$A$ has no inverse" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468510} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6428bf6c-1cd8-523e-89a2-bbd6aefca97b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467580} {:answer/id #uuid "49e7f113-867c-5ee0-a738-ba5b88651827" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467581}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467580} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e8c77e6-a0b4-526b-bf8e-a435b7b66ac1" :answer-field/key "$\\text{rank}(A)=n$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468511} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b22f319-2182-5f2f-984d-2c69a38c95bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467582} {:answer/id #uuid "f8184f79-583b-5721-92be-e461d3dc1a14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467583}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467582} :answer-field/id #uuid "d58f3fca-628f-5dd4-9837-348f91ad595e" :answer-field/key "All columns of $A$ are pivot columns" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468512}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2c600e13-fdff-5526-82d0-6659ac10dfc3" :question/math-academy-id "q-47587" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $$\n\\displaystyle \\,⇔\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A) &={R}^{n} \\\\ \\text{dim(Col}(A)) &=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\ \\text{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) &=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $A$ has no inverse.* $\\,✓$  \n\nIndeed,  a matrix $A$ is invertible if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $\\text{rank}(A)=n.$*$\\,\\times$\n\nSince our matrix is not invertible, according to the invertible matrix theorem, it must be $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne n.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then all columns of $A$ are pivot columns.*  $\\,\\times$\n\nSince $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne n$, it must be $\\text{dim(Col}(A))<n,$ which means that not all columns of $A$ are pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$A$ has no inverse” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342108 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e042c5e-e3ef-511f-b95b-58a232058836" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340102} {:answer/id #uuid "859cdad4-8ded-5774-9aec-7daebeff823d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -15 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340326} {:answer/id #uuid "8818494e-fcd8-5082-9a96-9ed2616431d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340347} {:answer/id #uuid "af3d06d6-f7a7-5b87-b458-af2ed75485a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340725} {:answer/id #uuid "d7714e60-73eb-5dc8-a41e-4a76cd230a52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 15 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341038}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341038} :answer-field/id #uuid "892def45-fd05-566e-afd6-be2b00ed2ed5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341620}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "56215786-6dd7-5900-942c-c24344ff27f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-73927" :question/problem "If $v=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$, then $3v=$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying each component of $v$ by $3,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3v & =3\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3\\cdot 0 \\\\ 3\\cdot 2 \\\\ 3\\cdot 5 \\\\ 3\\cdot (-1)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 15 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342109 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04c54bd8-230e-5991-b661-53cd75eaf2e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 15 \\\\ -20\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339165} {:answer/id #uuid "0af1a3d6-9497-53bd-80b5-88e5d7f8cc46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339223} {:answer/id #uuid "6dc337cc-06bf-5e73-80b3-0df5f3ffcd16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340099} {:answer/id #uuid "8170a3de-5ae6-56af-b0e1-1d9b907905e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340292} {:answer/id #uuid "e3067d48-3a49-55c1-8a8c-84c534f28233" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -15 \\\\ 20\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341138}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339165} :answer-field/id #uuid "cba8392b-14cc-5d45-a4cd-bb77082737a7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341738}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e4f125d7-bde6-5bbc-b86e-a1dc22a6397f" :question/math-academy-id "q-73929" :question/problem "If $w=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}$, then $5w=$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying each component of $w$ by $5,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5w & =5\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5\\cdot 1 \\\\ 5\\cdot (-1) \\\\ 5\\cdot 3 \\\\ 5\\cdot (-4)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 15 \\\\ -20\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342112 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43d96809-e3dd-5fef-aec9-43b2a849f964" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339725} {:answer/id #uuid "53143a70-d722-51cd-8e2b-e4e20cc2d282" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339893} {:answer/id #uuid "707f529c-3710-523a-9777-24e6935aad7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340126} {:answer/id #uuid "ea6b0a98-b813-579e-9675-d74b38ae8281" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341199} {:answer/id #uuid "f11c1ac8-7991-5f39-84b0-28a20d7bcaf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341253}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341253} :answer-field/id #uuid "eef3e121-56c7-5a3b-bf87-c4536c1b03a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341808}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7fa0bdb5-f053-5d67-8f95-d145fa39b1e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-73939" :question/problem "Let $a=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}$ and $b=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$ What is $(\\frac{1}{2}a)\\cdot b?$" :question/worked-solution "First, multiplying each component of $a$ by $\\frac{1}{2}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}a & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo compute the dot product, we add up the products of corresponding components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{1}{2}a)\\cdot b & =2\\cdot 5+(-1)\\cdot (-3)+1\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 0+5\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =10+3+1+0+10 \\\\  & =24\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342113 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4cee0a15-8f95-5c67-b97f-2df7a4828b00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339827} {:answer/id #uuid "5092076e-a330-582e-8b58-64e3bc1ee4d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339863} {:answer/id #uuid "54d19515-e8b8-55f6-bf08-b21031ad3105" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339907} {:answer/id #uuid "7b87dc60-ad14-50ea-8dac-947d0ec933d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340236} {:answer/id #uuid "e7ea377d-b28a-5fa3-afc4-d6ddc8b76c2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341174}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340236} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1082f34-5826-58d8-94b2-6eabf9e12ef6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341715}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9d756465-9173-5daf-942c-7abdf0168d3c" :question/math-academy-id "q-73941" :question/problem "Let $c=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ and $d=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}.$ What is $(-\\frac{1}{3}c)\\cdot d?$" :question/worked-solution "First, multiplying each component of $c$ by $-\\frac{1}{3}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{3}c & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo compute the dot product, we add up the products of corresponding components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-\\frac{1}{3}c)\\cdot d & =0\\cdot 9+2\\cdot 4+(-4)\\cdot (-2)+(-3)\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =0+8+8-3-6 \\\\  & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342114 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b05a743-0bc4-5712-84ed-0da6442c97a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339958} {:answer/id #uuid "866ae864-002f-535a-ba7d-88f2a4bebafa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340336} {:answer/id #uuid "8db5af6c-cf95-529a-8f4d-2e820009f178" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340402} {:answer/id #uuid "b4c799ed-4085-5b8e-8ad8-3e38d8f798a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340768} {:answer/id #uuid "cf423d8b-51d9-5633-86ea-e86786ef3cf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340971}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340336} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c128dfd-4307-5e43-a63b-f8aa0d49e374" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341455}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e030b11b-7d8c-5bb3-95d3-2268959b30a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-73948" :question/problem "Let $v=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ 2x \\\\ 4 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}$ and $w=\\begin{bmatrix}3x \\\\ -3 \\\\ x \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$\nIf $v\\cdot w=-2$ and $x>0$, find the value of $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Starting from the equation $v\\cdot w=-2,$ we compute the dot product in terms of $x$ and then solve for $x$ in the resulting equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot w & =-2 \\\\ x\\cdot 3x+2x\\cdot (-3)+4\\cdot x+(-5)\\cdot 2 & =-2 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-6x+4x-10 & =-2 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-2x-8 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the quadratic formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{-(-2)\\pm \\sqrt{(-2)^{2}-4(3)(-8)}}{2(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pm \\sqrt{100}}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pm 10}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\pm 5}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get two solutions, ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{4}{3}$ and ${x}_{2}=2.$ Since we need $x>0$, our final answer is $x=2$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342115 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e6d2d84-09cc-54f0-8421-d83f6ddef14d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339259} {:answer/id #uuid "4ff10e4f-a950-5386-bebb-cd13c7ed95cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339856} {:answer/id #uuid "7409f5a7-2d41-5eb1-89ec-5e541d8fad83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340156} {:answer/id #uuid "9f8ec39e-0abf-580d-96bb-85070bd2da2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340571} {:answer/id #uuid "bfea793d-91a0-5f45-ad3f-c1a205bf1dd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340840}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340571} :answer-field/id #uuid "add42bb3-f82f-527d-bf73-b41e64fbfe31" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341683}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "64baab11-7178-5faa-a751-966ea0fbee6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-73949" :question/problem "Let $l=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ x \\\\ 2 \\\\ x \\\\ 2x\\end{bmatrix}$ and $m=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ x \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.$\nIf $l\\cdot m=3$ and $x>3$, find the value of $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Starting from the equation $l\\cdot m=3,$ we compute the dot product in terms of $x$ and then solve for $x$ in the resulting equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}l\\cdot m & =3 \\\\ 5\\cdot 1+x\\cdot x+2\\cdot 4+x\\cdot (-1)+2x\\cdot (-3) & =3 \\\\ 5+{x}^{2}+8-x-6x & =3 \\\\ {x}^{2}-7x+13 & =3 \\\\ {x}^{2}-7x+10 & =0 \\\\ (x-5)(x-2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe get two solutions, ${x}_{1}=5$ and ${x}_{2}=2.$ Since we need $x>3$, our final answer is $x=5$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344968 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "360cc03a-3f39-5879-9a88-a61073b7fcf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A2}$, $\\text{A4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342683} {:answer/id #uuid "6d6880fc-5f2b-5192-95d6-4d52a478dfb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A2}$, $\\text{A5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343177} {:answer/id #uuid "71d6a532-cd4b-5d34-ae27-3901b1065d79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A3}$, $\\text{A4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343222} {:answer/id #uuid "ca10db7b-bf57-5c5b-a421-62ab3bb870b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A3}$, $\\text{A5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344014} {:answer/id #uuid "ea3d0561-a8a8-5898-828f-77cac082232d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A2}$, $\\text{A8}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344289}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342683} :answer-field/id #uuid "86bd575b-d1b5-591b-a355-2d1fcad9bf66" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344730}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c4dc6297-c39f-58c6-a8af-023dc6a275e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-74671" :question/problem "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement:* \n\n*If $x$ is a vector such that $-x+w=w$ for some $w\\in V$, then $x=0$* \n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x+w & =w &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ x+(-x+w) & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{adding }x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (x+(-x))+w & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ 0+w & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ w & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{axiom  A3}\\,] \\\\ w+(-w) & =x+w+(-w) &  & [\\,\\text{adding }-w\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ w+(-w) & =x+(w+(-w)) &  & [\\,\\text{axioms  A2}\\,] \\\\ 0 & =x+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,] \\\\ 0 & =x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom  A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the vector space axioms, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x+w & =w &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ x+(-x+w) & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{adding }x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (x+(-x))+w & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A2}\\,\\,] \\\\ 0+w & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ w & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{axiom  A3}\\,] \\\\ w+(-w) & =x+w+(-w) &  & [\\,\\text{adding }-w\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ w+(-w) & =x+(w+(-w)) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom  A2}\\,] \\\\ 0 & =x+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A4}\\,\\,] \\\\ 0 & =x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom  A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344987 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22e86af6-dc09-5728-af39-ea9ad098ae58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342528} {:answer/id #uuid "5d603301-b7c0-544b-b506-9c4a65d6cdae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343021} {:answer/id #uuid "89b97186-4fec-59be-a7c9-cc47c84df4f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343435} {:answer/id #uuid "e0ec6d4b-1ee9-5b64-8eaf-562a6b069f61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344214} {:answer/id #uuid "fe79acec-9798-50b6-a67c-5d451e8a5963" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344476}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344476} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ca04bb4-7748-5354-8361-af71cdae5fba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344521}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b184b945-0cbf-54e5-bc87-5c6a9c59df68" :question/math-academy-id "q-74867" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$ and the vector $b=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2k \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find the value of $k$ such that $b\\in \\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "If $b\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then we must have $Ab=0.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2k \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}4k-8 \\\\ 2k-4\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4k-8 &=0 \\\\ 2k-4 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344988 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "139ee80c-6e6e-531b-a6b8-99112c3e1abb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{bmatrix}5{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\,:\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342410} {:answer/id #uuid "3b64258e-e02b-59a9-874c-a387dbf35e5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{2}-5{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\,:\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342725} {:answer/id #uuid "8638435e-1b5c-5f83-bf5a-e7216da4208f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{bmatrix}5{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\,:\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343390} {:answer/id #uuid "9feaf2b5-7a06-5f65-9627-c410de97218e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343649} {:answer/id #uuid "b43c1faf-0fd9-599c-8b40-f816145be536" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\,:\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343817}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342725} :answer-field/id #uuid "67b07404-4457-5215-9465-0363a04266f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344670}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "585342a5-4f43-526c-91d5-902d1e3aac63" :question/math-academy-id "q-74870" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -10 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 15\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "We need to solve the equation $Ax=0.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -10 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 15\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 15\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ 0 &=0 \\\\ 0 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is ${x}_{1}$, and we have two free variables, ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ in terms of ${x}_{2}$  and ${x}_{3}.$\n\nFrom the first equation we get ${x}_{1}=2{x}_{2}-5{x}_{3},$ so the set of all the solutions of $Ax=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{2}-5{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\,:\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344989 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "170a6a8b-0a94-5182-b976-bd0b41e8fe28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{bmatrix}3{x}_{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342442} {:answer/id #uuid "b220f0b0-24d4-501f-958a-b59cb6183ced" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{bmatrix}-3{x}_{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343802} {:answer/id #uuid "ccca0f14-75d2-51d0-9c72-dc0eae6278da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{bmatrix}3{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344044} {:answer/id #uuid "dbf57b16-c151-502c-b06d-4bddc574b353" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344167} {:answer/id #uuid "e60b0611-b8ae-57e8-9414-9ab2f893e68c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{bmatrix}-3{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344259}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186343802} :answer-field/id #uuid "6727db5e-bd9d-5baf-8e3c-10a6c913aa52" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344668}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0ac77401-4e26-5c21-810e-811c018a9f7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-74872" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 9 & -9 \\\\ 6 & -18 & 18 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "We need to solve the equation $Ax=0.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 9 & -9 \\\\ 6 & -18 & 18 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 9\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 6 & -18 & 18 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 9\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-6){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 9\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ 0 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, and we have one free variable, ${x}_{3}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ in terms of ${x}_{3}.$\n\nThe second equation tells us that ${x}_{2}=0.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-3(0)+3{x}_{3}=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-3{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nSo the set of all the solutions of $Ax=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={\\begin{bmatrix}-3{x}_{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\,:\\,{x}_{3}\\in R}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345025 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09edbcaf-e507-56c2-9601-97a969f32090" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442767} {:answer/id #uuid "0c61635a-16c4-5875-a03d-2914bf2b487b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442768} {:answer/id #uuid "2decce7e-2100-5b81-a206-46546723c381" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442771} {:answer/id #uuid "4143e3f3-49a8-557d-b984-d646890798bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442773} {:answer/id #uuid "a5fbafaa-f05c-5762-8d2f-0ad19854c541" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442781}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442773} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7cace19-2ac2-5d38-9b8e-8da19509dd92" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344840}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8e44b5dc-345c-58d4-a170-3fddfd0702d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-75073" :question/problem "Consider the matrix \n$$\n\\displaystyle W=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -6 & 9 & -2 \\\\ 8 & -12 & 10\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$ \nFind a basis $B$ of  $\\text{Col}(W).$" :question/worked-solution "In order to find a basis of $\\text{Col}(W),$ we reduce the matrix $W$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -6 & 9 & -2 \\\\ 8 & -12 & 10\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 8 & -12 & 10\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to linearly independent vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the $1$st and $3$rd columns are pivot columns, while the $2$nd column is a non-pivot column.\n\nRemember that we need to pick the pivot columns from the *original matrix*, not from the reduced one. \n\nThe $1$st and $3$rd columns from the original matrix are ${w}_{1}$ and ${w}_{3}.$ So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(W)$ is $\\{{w}_{1},{w}_{3}\\},$ that is to say, \n\n$$\nB=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345026 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f71b28a-eef0-50b5-b4b5-85ae1a337b71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342499} {:answer/id #uuid "28b83eaa-9f9a-5888-a2aa-1155dad0a14b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{{}{u}_{1},{u}_{3}\\text{}}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Col}(U)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342579} {:answer/id #uuid "35d6e4cc-ad73-5db8-bcdb-9c95d86e599c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342681} {:answer/id #uuid "5a8dc9f5-497a-5697-aed3-a18f39d92052" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342995} {:answer/id #uuid "cbb60c97-7060-599d-a7c0-7dc790f9f8b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344031}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342499} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5c1f721-ec7c-5bf5-b0ff-1e3f5a8737f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344862}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0c9d82d6-6531-5354-9b3b-01e8f3d44990" :question/math-academy-id "q-75083" :question/problem "The matrix $U$ is given below. Let ${u}_{1}$, ${u}_{2}$, and ${u}_{3}$ be the respective columns of $U.$\nDetermine if $B=\\text{{}{u}_{1},{u}_{3}\\text{}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Col}(U).$ \nIf that is the case, find ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{3}$, where ${u}_{2}={x}_{1}{u}_{1}+{x}_{3}{u}_{3}.$\n\n$$\nU=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ -4 & 8 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reduce the matrix $U$ to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ -4 & 8 & 8\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=\\left(-\\frac{1}{4}\\right){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st and $3$rd columns. So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(U)$ is ${{u}_{1},{u}_{3}},$ that is to say,\n\n$$\nB={\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}}.\n$$\n\nNow, since the $2$nd column of the reduced matrix is a non-pivot column, then the entries in that column tell us the coefficients needed to express ${u}_{2}$ as a linear combination of all the other columns in the original matrix. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}}_{{u}_{2}}=\\underbrace{(-2)}_{{x}_{1}}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}}_{{u}_{1}}+\\underbrace{(0)}_{{x}_{3}}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}}_{{u}_{3}}.\n$$\n\nThis gives us ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{3}=(-2)\\cdot 0=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345138 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68d0aa0d-d15b-53b1-b587-29d21d242662" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343134} {:answer/id #uuid "8454df55-5625-586c-8f0c-e59a199cf2f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343370} {:answer/id #uuid "897525de-2820-5f27-9f87-c7818129d1a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343431} {:answer/id #uuid "ace01dcb-3f03-5590-92b8-6bbe03249e1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343761} {:answer/id #uuid "c4178081-bdf7-5733-b5be-9444a4cfd6f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{{}{d}_{1},{d}_{2}\\text{}}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Col}(D)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343961}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186343134} :answer-field/id #uuid "4cf34ce4-972f-542d-98a2-41b9843bb493" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344622}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "29f3d15c-3699-5650-acaa-cf842bca8086" :question/math-academy-id "q-75944" :question/problem "The matrix $D$ is given below. Let ${d}_{1}$, ${d}_{2}$, and ${d}_{3}$ be the respective columns of $D.$ Determine if $B=\\text{{}{d}_{1},{d}_{2}\\text{}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Col}(D).$ If that is the case, find ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$, where ${d}_{3}={x}_{1}{d}_{1}+{x}_{2}{d}_{2}.$\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -7 & -17\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reduce the matrix $D$ to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -7 & -17\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -16\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=\\left(-\\frac{1}{8}\\right){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st and $2$nd columns. So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(D)$ is ${{d}_{1},{d}_{2}},$ that is to say,\n\n$$\nB={\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}}.\n$$\n\nNow, since the $3$rd column of the reduced matrix is a non-pivot column, then the entries in that column tell us the coefficients needed to express ${d}_{3}$ as a linear combination of all the other columns in the original matrix. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -17\\end{bmatrix}}_{{d}_{3}}=\\underbrace{(3)}_{{x}_{1}}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}}_{{d}_{1}}+\\underbrace{(2)}_{{x}_{2}}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}}_{{d}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nThis gives us ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=3\\cdot 2=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345139 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "016024ef-c03f-5e15-8220-be9fb68e1bd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342260} {:answer/id #uuid "094fd71c-9a23-5d25-860d-bc340d895bbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342315} {:answer/id #uuid "3e7a7b2d-982a-5570-b5f8-b8e34bf4d03c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342753} {:answer/id #uuid "6ed580a2-4268-5399-96f5-ea373b9218d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343193} {:answer/id #uuid "8255c71a-6cc1-58b7-8b63-f24165915a0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{{}{p}_{1},{p}_{2}\\text{}}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Col}(P)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343355}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342753} :answer-field/id #uuid "3033d739-a4dc-5f2c-8494-cf265f068411" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344578}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "edfd11b7-178d-5b9f-89aa-f777ae4db963" :question/math-academy-id "q-75946" :question/problem "The matrix $P$ is given below. Let ${p}_{1}$, ${p}_{2}$, and ${p}_{3}$ be the respective columns of $P.$\nDetermine if $B=\\text{{}{p}_{1},{p}_{2}\\text{}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Col}(P).$ \nIf that is the case, find ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$, where ${p}_{3}={x}_{1}{p}_{1}+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}.$\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reduce the matrix $P$ to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st and $2$nd columns. So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(P)$ is $\\{{p}_{1},{p}_{2}\\},$ that is to say,\n\n$$\nB=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}.\n$$\n\nNow, since the $3$rd column of the reduced matrix is a non-pivot column, then the entries in that column tell us the coefficients needed to express ${p}_{3}$ as a linear combination of all the other columns in the original matrix. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}}_{{p}_{3}}=\\underbrace{(-2)}_{{x}_{1}}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{{p}_{1}}+\\underbrace{(1)}_{{x}_{2}}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}}_{{p}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nThis gives us ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=(-2)\\cdot 1=-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345143 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32f287f2-7edb-54c9-83f8-d6a429304e1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342666} {:answer/id #uuid "54012245-c061-5945-8365-5fb96a1bba3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342937} {:answer/id #uuid "5b1e59c1-2c67-56da-a21f-63f2eaa8fa17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{{}{w}_{1},{w}_{3}\\text{}}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Col}(W)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342999} {:answer/id #uuid "9055039c-4784-5800-8ebe-48c648a6f6f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343499} {:answer/id #uuid "b2c372df-a7fc-55c4-aeb2-27fc2c39d58a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343808}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342937} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b4e5f9d-166d-57e6-b089-2301e828158d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344764}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8e38527f-7273-52c9-bec3-d94fc3af2837" :question/math-academy-id "q-75956" :question/problem "The matrix $W$ is given below. Let ${w}_{1}$, ${w}_{2}$, and ${w}_{3}$ be the respective columns of $W.$\nDetermine if $B=\\text{{}{w}_{1},{w}_{3}\\text{}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Col}(W).$ \nIf that is the case, find ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{3}$, where ${w}_{2}={x}_{1}{w}_{1}+{x}_{3}{w}_{3}.$\n\n$$\nW=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -6 & 4 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reduce the matrix $W$ to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -6 & 4 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 9\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 9\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st and $3$rd columns. So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(W)$ is $\\{{w}_{1},{w}_{3}\\},$ that is to say,\n\n$$\nB=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}.\n$$\n\nNow, since the $2$nd column of the reduced matrix is a non-pivot column, then the entries in that column tell us the coefficients needed to express ${w}_{2}$ as a linear combination of all the other columns in the original matrix. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}}_{{w}_{2}}=\\underbrace{(-3)}_{{x}_{1}}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}}_{{w}_{1}}+\\underbrace{(0)}_{{x}_{3}}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}}_{{w}_{3}}.\n$$\n\nThis gives us ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{3}=(-3)\\cdot 0=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345149 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56326641-cf59-57eb-b78e-0a02a8992ad0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342955} {:answer/id #uuid "699ab4f9-6336-5399-980c-dc32fd2b7101" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343140} {:answer/id #uuid "961a3ec8-f1bb-5d87-a172-a8257890a9cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343551} {:answer/id #uuid "e3d6beb2-7ff7-5c87-91be-6fa2a12c62ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344239} {:answer/id #uuid "96a3e6f1-81c0-56ef-815f-d0a58729ca14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\{{h}_{1},{h}_{2}\\}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Col}(H)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442780}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442780} :answer-field/id #uuid "9df7a474-f23c-56da-ad81-c35426f28ffc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344768}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e2ee7dc8-6fbf-5fd7-b2a6-20aab9680dc7" :question/math-academy-id "q-75977" :question/problem "The matrix $H$ is given below. Let ${h}_{1}$, ${h}_{2}$,  ${h}_{3}$ and ${h}_{4}$ be the respective columns of $H.$\nDetermine if $B=\\text{{}{h}_{1},{h}_{2}\\text{}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Col}(H).$ \nIf that is the case, find ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$, where ${h}_{4}={x}_{1}{h}_{1}+{x}_{2}{h}_{2}.$ \n\n$$\nH=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 & 12 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 9 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reduce the matrix $H$ to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}H & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 & 12 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 9 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 9 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd columns. So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(H)$ is $\\{{h}_{1},{h}_{2},{h}_{3}\\}.$ \n\nTherefore, we conclude that $B=\\{{h}_{1},{h}_{2}\\}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Col}(H).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345151 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3214ac66-089e-5f1a-b5f5-27127d89af81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342662} {:answer/id #uuid "5e6f8a38-0a5a-5b8d-9bbd-8d6b55a7767b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343032} {:answer/id #uuid "69df0ecf-34a7-5ab2-a85a-47fd55e5f70c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343142} {:answer/id #uuid "fd9fef81-c774-530d-bce3-3ec15ebb79e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344469} {:answer/id #uuid "f635b87e-9ad6-595e-8ac8-cf7446521d1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{3}\\}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Col}(V)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423617}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423617} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab78a2e2-73c6-516c-bb41-33e676435ed4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344794}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c466a2ff-d594-54f8-8655-5aeb347fd10d" :question/math-academy-id "q-75980" :question/problem "The matrix $V$ is given below. Let ${v}_{1}$, ${v}_{2}$,  ${v}_{3}$ and ${v}_{4}$ be the respective columns of $V.$\nDetermine if $B=\\text{{}{v}_{1},{v}_{3}\\text{}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Col}(V).$ \nIf that is the case, find ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{3}$, where ${v}_{2}={x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}.$ \n\n$$\nV=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 & -6 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 10 & 20 & 10 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reduce the matrix $V$ to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 & -6 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 10 & 20 & 10 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\left(-\\frac{1}{3}\\right){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 10 & 20 & 10 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 10 & 20 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{10}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st, $2$nd, and $4$th columns. So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(V)$ is $\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{4}\\}.$ \n\nTherefore, we conclude that $B=\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{3}\\}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Col}(V).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348208 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0038a274-1fea-5c60-93f2-4e1f0aa3d0bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468244} {:answer/id #uuid "483dc84e-dfea-55fa-a0cb-de1ae000bf1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468245}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186468244} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2201cc9-18d3-571c-ae72-347981af2222" :answer-field/key "$A$ is **not** invertible" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468843} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb16210a-cfa0-52ec-956b-46bc4659a344" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468246} {:answer/id #uuid "5cc5591d-8321-5239-af2f-da46eeeba04e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468247}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186468247} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f0d4571-9f8e-5b3c-8a20-6f5a2b8194b8" :answer-field/key "$\\text{rank}(A)=n$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468844} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38651f09-b1dd-5820-93c3-99e2657a2fbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468248} {:answer/id #uuid "3f51e910-74bd-5148-8e34-b3c363679221" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468249}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186468249} :answer-field/id #uuid "020dec00-eb40-52fb-acf8-97681452e138" :answer-field/key "$\\text{Col}(A)={\\mathbb{R}}^{n}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468845}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e25ee2d5-6236-5cb7-ae46-36798fde6f33" :question/math-academy-id "q-79334" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then  $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $$\n\\displaystyle \\,⇔\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A) &={R}^{n} \\\\ \\text{dim(Col}(A)) &=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\ \\text{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) &=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $A$ is **not** invertible.* $\\,\\times$\n\nBy the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ we must have that $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $\\text{rank}(A)=n.$* $\\,✓$ \n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{rank}(A)=\\text{dim(Col}(A))=n.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n}.$* $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{rank}(A)=n$; $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n}$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348209 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e0e3b4d-76d8-5cbd-90c5-fca2f4d2fe65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345611} {:answer/id #uuid "1e90027c-95de-50a1-8923-ce31ce3d2313" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345618} {:answer/id #uuid "4038465c-abf2-5ed6-9c88-95500bd0b19f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345902} {:answer/id #uuid "cf17d181-6a72-5a6a-bae2-520b2dbc3c35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347164} {:answer/id #uuid "f71c67cc-176a-5401-80d5-3e97ea441762" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347541}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345902} :answer-field/id #uuid "334d8fb3-3204-5b82-b1f9-48d1d1b54725" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347690}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3b68de97-54e7-561a-89fd-56e4e1f74d49" :question/math-academy-id "q-79336" :question/problem "Let $Q$ be a $5\\times 8$ matrix that has $5$ pivot columns. What is the dimension of the null space of $Q?$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\text{dim(Null}(Q))$ is the number of non-pivot columns in $Q.$ \n\nSince $Q$ has $8$ columns and $5$ of them are pivots, then the number of non-pivot columns in $Q$ is \n\n$$\n8-5=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{dim(Null}(Q))=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348210 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "312c6d20-1c2c-5d6c-8b8e-cf23e71760b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345786} {:answer/id #uuid "45f68372-7412-515e-9814-e6c0f7a8c6df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345962} {:answer/id #uuid "494853f8-4935-5a39-a8d0-6626a696cd34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345978} {:answer/id #uuid "5e485b0d-d5b8-51f0-ab8f-2f8a805ffe49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346164} {:answer/id #uuid "83d7b447-77de-56ac-bfd7-234b2ea324f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346495}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345962} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ff6cd6c-1a28-5518-928d-911043fbb6bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347777}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d57f1c7b-d650-5ce4-a519-f725671f3653" :question/math-academy-id "q-79339" :question/problem "If $D$ is a $6\\times 10$ matrix that has $8$ **non-pivot** columns, then $\\text{dim(Null}(D))=$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\text{dim(Null}(D))$ is the number of non-pivot columns in $D.$\n\nSince we are told that $D$ has $8$ non-pivot columns, we have \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(D))=8.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351223 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f9ec959-6c9a-57e1-ae0a-6a076a7d5def" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469224} {:answer/id #uuid "2d4ab090-ec29-550d-ba58-e9d28247fdd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469225}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186469224} :answer-field/id #uuid "5af42925-d1d8-558c-98a2-b6afb6006d99" :answer-field/key "$U=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470224} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f85509fa-72b0-5356-9281-0306a2883679" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469226} {:answer/id #uuid "8d077489-acb7-511c-ba14-a31d55734b32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469227}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186469227} :answer-field/id #uuid "6cf7eb21-0d7a-553e-8a84-78201bbb4178" :answer-field/key "$V=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470225} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd229fc2-3cb9-5263-8bc2-1ad4e67230df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469228} {:answer/id #uuid "d68af363-ffa3-5154-bebb-0a3e9fd71962" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469229}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186469229} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5130a91-d1f8-5b78-832a-6465f79297b4" :answer-field/key "$W=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470226}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "25a9c5a2-c2b4-580a-a454-817fa98a8c5d" :question/math-academy-id "q-81109" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are orthonormal?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of the given sets as \n$\\{{u}_{1},{u}_{2},{u}_{3}\\},$ \n$\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}\\},$ and \n$\\{{w}_{1},{w}_{2}\\},$ respectively. \n\nThe sets $U,V,$ and $W$ are orthonormal if the following conditions on each set hold:\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle \\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2} &=0 \\\\ {u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{3} &=0 \\\\ {u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{3} &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\text{and}\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{1} &=1 \\\\ {u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{2} &=1 \\\\ {u}_{3}\\cdot {u}_{3} &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle {v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2}=0\\,\\text{and}\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1} &=1 \\\\ {v}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2} &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle \\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2} &=0 \\\\ {w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{3} &=0 \\\\ {w}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{3} &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\text{and}\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{1} &=1 \\\\ {w}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{2} &=1 \\\\ {w}_{3}\\cdot {w}_{3} &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- For the set $U,$ notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{1} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}=1+25+4=30\\ne 1 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $U$ is not an orthonormal set.\n\n- For the set $V,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}=-\\frac{6}{13}+\\frac{6}{13}=0 & ✓ \\\\ {v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1} & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{4}{13}+\\frac{9}{13}=1 & ✓ \\\\ {v}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{9}{13}+\\frac{4}{13}=1 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the set $V$ is orthonormal.\n\n- For the set $W,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{18}}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{18}}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{18}}=0 & ✓ \\\\ {w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{1} & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{4}{6}+\\frac{1}{6}=1 & ✓ \\\\ {w}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}=1 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the set $W$ is orthonormal.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"$V$ and $W$ only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351226 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09f37115-979c-5246-9d94-c67fef08cc33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348529} {:answer/id #uuid "0be4924f-2bcb-5e68-bb91-0b202ac2e3f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348547} {:answer/id #uuid "0e2caaa8-3b3b-5917-9117-2c00ca744780" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348569} {:answer/id #uuid "36e30243-1bcb-54b4-a974-3246d1b94ec9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348940} {:answer/id #uuid "93af1e85-3ecc-55b6-b207-b559abeda572" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349767}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348940} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb859c54-ca8c-559d-b875-da4c3b754acf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351032}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "69162096-003d-5b5d-8f8d-d7d2695037b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-81114" :question/problem "Consider the **orthonormal** set $U$ below. By adding a new vector $x=[{x}_{1},\\,{x}_{2}]^{T},$ extend the set so that it forms an **orthonormal** basis of ${R}^{2}.$ What is the value of $|{x}_{1}|+|{x}_{2}|?$\n\n$$\nU=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vector of $U$ as ${u}_{1}.$ To extend the given set to an orthonormal basis of ${R}^{2}$, we need to find a second vector $x$ such that $‖x‖=1,$ and\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}\\cdot x=0\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{x}_{1}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{x}_{2}=0.\n$$\n\nFrom the above equation, we get ${x}_{1}=-{x}_{2}.$\n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{2}=1,$ we obtain the vector \n$$\n\\displaystyle x=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$ \n\nNow, we need to normalize $x.$ Notice that $‖x‖=\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}=\\sqrt{2}.$ So, we normalize $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{‖x‖}=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, an orthonormal basis of ${R}^{2}$ is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}.\n$$\n\nFinally, $$\n\\displaystyle |{x}_{1}|+|{x}_{2}|=|-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}|+|\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}|=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}}=\\sqrt{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351227 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "189d2399-778e-5f91-9ce1-32d37b562b37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348652} {:answer/id #uuid "2f6bc17c-b29b-5b6a-825f-b7920485b355" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348866} {:answer/id #uuid "38134468-105d-5545-b17a-c9d893973845" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348954} {:answer/id #uuid "80bacf94-e6b0-55c9-8313-8118522cc9ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349631} {:answer/id #uuid "ce2f35df-6285-56ba-86dc-c65951a79230" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350260}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348954} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3379fdb-e83b-5562-9116-6ddff065a38c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351134}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9eae85b5-72a3-53d6-aeb1-1aeb5a7806f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-81115" :question/problem "Consider the **orthonormal** set $U$ below. By adding a new vector $x=[{x}_{1},\\,{x}_{2}]^{T},$ extend the set so that it forms an **orthonormal** basis of ${R}^{2}.$ What is the value of $|{x}_{1}|+|{x}_{2}|?$\n\n$$\nU={\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vector of $U$ as ${u}_{1}.$ To extend the given set to an orthonormal basis of ${R}^{2}$, we need to find a second vector $x$ such that $‖x‖=1,$ and\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}\\cdot x=0\\,⟹\\,\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}{x}_{1}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}{x}_{2}=0.\n$$\n\nFrom the above equation, we get ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2}.$\n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{2}=-2,$ we obtain the vector \n$$\n\\displaystyle x=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$ \n\nNow, we need to normalize $x.$ Notice that $‖x‖=\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}=\\sqrt{5}.$ So, we normalize $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{‖x‖}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, an orthonormal basis of ${R}^{2}$ is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, $$\n\\displaystyle |{x}_{1}|+|{x}_{2}|=|\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}|+|-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}|=\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351228 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3dd2f2a3-5aab-5869-b6f3-a577fb595015" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{35}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349006} {:answer/id #uuid "58be237d-ce4d-5668-82d3-3c25e17c744a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{7}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349261} {:answer/id #uuid "87a944e7-db24-5023-a626-63f6ac1039b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{35}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349683} {:answer/id #uuid "cbc1942d-0817-5d0e-a085-26d103200d73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{35}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350239} {:answer/id #uuid "e5492ef3-ea24-5af8-b30f-dab1b019a1e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350460}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186350239} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c3572e5-1026-5c3a-b665-18f041e53fc1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350922}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7ee661be-3380-50f2-9670-d857c4eed458" :question/math-academy-id "q-81117" :question/problem "Consider the **orthonormal** set $U$ below. By adding a new vector $x=[{x}_{1},\\,{x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3}]^{T},$ extend the set so that it forms an **orthonormal** basis of ${R}^{3}.$ What is the value of $|{x}_{1}|+|{x}_{2}|+|{x}_{3}|?$\n\n$$\nU={\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{14}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{14}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{14}}\\end{bmatrix}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $U$ as ${u}_{1},\\,{u}_{2}.$ To extend the given set to an orthonormal basis of ${R}^{3}$, we need to find a third vector $x$ such that $‖x‖=1,$ and\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot x &=0 \\\\ {u}_{2}\\cdot x &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}{x}_{2}+\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{14}}{x}_{1}+\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{14}}{x}_{2}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{14}}{x}_{3} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system above and reduce it to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{14}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{14}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{14}} & 0\\end{array}\\right] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:=\\sqrt{10}\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{2}:=\\sqrt{14}\\cdot {R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & -1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are two pivot columns ($1$st and $2$nd). Thus, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=3{x}_{3}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n-2{x}_{1}+3(3{x}_{3})+{x}_{3}=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=5{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}5{x}_{3} \\\\ 3{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{3}=1,$ we obtain the vector \n$$\n\\displaystyle x=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$ \n\nNow, we need to normalize $x.$ Notice that $‖x‖=\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+{3}^{2}+{1}^{2}}=\\sqrt{35}.$ So, we normalize $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{‖x‖}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{35}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{35}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{35}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, an orthonormal basis of ${R}^{3}$ is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{14}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{14}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{14}}\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{35}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{35}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{35}}\\end{bmatrix}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, $$\n\\displaystyle |{x}_{1}|+|{x}_{2}|+|{x}_{3}|=|\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{35}}|+|\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{35}}|+|\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{35}}|=\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{35}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351421 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eec7f9d0-6840-5a0d-9763-9d79e17c960b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469272} {:answer/id #uuid "e17563c3-bef4-5de4-bfa8-3abc6787cdbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469273}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186469272} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2536c2a-97f0-5d07-85f7-dac71d9a3595" :answer-field/key "$U={\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470248} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c791f35-ef8d-5d1b-ac20-4bba4ba088a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469274} {:answer/id #uuid "42ccffe9-aa3a-51d7-a314-a985b53a16d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469275}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186469274} :answer-field/id #uuid "c20072e3-cac0-5e39-9977-109f479878d1" :answer-field/key "$V={\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470249} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff210b55-f992-57f3-b9b8-5b982205db1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469276} {:answer/id #uuid "9b795f5c-7553-5cf0-835e-232adb57839c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469277}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186469277} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e0a6fc6-975c-5d4a-a9d1-779257288450" :answer-field/key "$W={\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470250}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0e6a1e4f-2315-5270-b1fa-4652e5933f97" :question/math-academy-id "q-82396" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are orthogonal?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of the given sets as \n${{u}_{1},{u}_{2},{u}_{3}},$\n${{v}_{1},{v}_{2}},$ and \n${{w}_{1},{w}_{2},{w}_{3}},$ respectively. \n\nThe sets $U,V,$ and $W$ are orthogonal if the following conditions on each set hold:\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle {u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0,\\,{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{3}=0,\\,{u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{3}=0.\n$$\n\n- ${v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2}=0.$\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle {w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2}=0,\\,{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{3}=0,\\,{w}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{3}=0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- For the set $U,$ notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=-10-3+0=-13\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $U$ is not an orthogonal set.\n\n- For the set $V,$ notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=-18-2=-20\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $V$ is not an orthogonal set.\n\n- For the set $W,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}=2-1-1=0 & ✓ \\\\ {w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{3} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=0-1+1=0 & ✓ \\\\ {w}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{3} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=0+1-1=0 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the set $W$ is orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"$W$ only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351422 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be5862e6-b730-5e81-9ac1-5e844249d701" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469278} {:answer/id #uuid "654dd76b-a128-5d4e-b986-b07234a9d3c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469279}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186469279} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c6dc41f-cfa7-5461-a976-ac251c6b54e5" :answer-field/key "$U={\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470251} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e4af0f3-7d42-5e9a-abb1-c42b4f5355c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469280} {:answer/id #uuid "bd22712f-03ea-5666-af1b-1402b2b37d3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469281}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186469281} :answer-field/id #uuid "24699510-dda2-5446-ac6e-65cc0cd53489" :answer-field/key "$V={\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470252} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ac75cde-6eb1-56e3-9185-ae7e5ed25b9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469282} {:answer/id #uuid "66347df5-2c1c-5bb6-89a7-f5ea0bcdf181" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469283}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186469282} :answer-field/id #uuid "34b6086a-d4e7-5d21-9eec-909a989af9d6" :answer-field/key "$W={\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470253}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c7632fcb-d145-5958-9540-44c860cfa586" :question/math-academy-id "q-82397" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are orthogonal?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of the given sets as \n${{u}_{1},{u}_{2},{u}_{3}},$ \n${{v}_{1},{v}_{2}},$ and \n${{w}_{1},{w}_{2}},$ respectively. \n\nThe sets $U,V,$ and $W$ are orthogonal if the following conditions on each set hold:\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle {u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0,\\,{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{3}=0,\\,{u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{3}=0.\n$$\n\n- ${v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2}=0.$\n\n- ${w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2}=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- For the set $U,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}=-1+3-1-1=0 & ✓ \\\\ {u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{3} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=1+0-2+1=0 & ✓ \\\\ {u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{3} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=-1+0+2-1=0 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the set $U$ is orthogonal.\n\n- For the set $V,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=2-1-1=0 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the set $V$ is orthogonal.\n\n- For the set $W,$ notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}=-15+24=9\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $W$ is not an orthogonal set.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"$U$ and $V$ only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351423 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b974feb-5457-574d-a527-ebd86a5e5813" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469284} {:answer/id #uuid "d4583b7f-a4ce-5f0e-bde1-2305fb803d32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469285}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186469284} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c04baba-bbb6-50c8-ad0a-506d8f8bf90f" :answer-field/key "$U={\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470254} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de462187-00a2-5c0a-8f94-af38fffbe0c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469286} {:answer/id #uuid "a974d9f6-4c7d-5c1e-a776-2b79fb0fd47b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469287}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186469286} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6947177-0e2d-5291-b8f3-8ab7a401723f" :answer-field/key "$V={\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470255} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ce4a16d-c13c-5ce1-91da-8761f7a9a9c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469288} {:answer/id #uuid "dc21e406-b931-5622-8c7f-f6a3c426155e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469289}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186469289} :answer-field/id #uuid "24a51c46-911d-55ae-a9b0-cd6fdec63972" :answer-field/key "$W={\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470256}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2c1e164f-769d-52d4-a09c-f8474e7b2368" :question/math-academy-id "q-82401" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are orthonormal?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of the given sets as \n${{u}_{1},{u}_{2}},$\n${{v}_{1},{v}_{2}},$ and \n${{w}_{1},{w}_{2}}$, respectively. \n\nThe sets $U,V,$ and $W$ are orthonormal if the following conditions on each set hold:\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle {u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0\\,\\text{and}\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{1} &=1 \\\\ {u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{2} &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle {v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2}=0\\,\\text{and}\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1} &=1 \\\\ {v}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2} &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle {w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2}=0\\,\\text{and}\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{1} &=1 \\\\ {w}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{2} &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- For the set $U,$ notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{1} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=1+1=2\\ne 1 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $U$ is not an orthonormal set.\n\n- For the set $V,$ notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=0+\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $V$ is not an orthonormal set.\n\n- For the set $W,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=0+0=0 & ✓ \\\\ {w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{1} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=1+0=1 & ✓ \\\\ {w}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=0+1=1 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the set $W$ is orthonormal.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"$W$ only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351535 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c093387-dd3a-57fc-9e3f-4c7d701bbf43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469308} {:answer/id #uuid "176aa2ed-e6ac-570d-9901-4a949990fefc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469309}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186469309} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf0364b8-59fa-5366-a895-e2c63cf5360e" :answer-field/key "$U={\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470266} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f17293f1-9f27-550b-852c-f9600bba572e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469310} {:answer/id #uuid "cb40de30-bab0-5067-aa1b-eaab8f18473e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469311}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186469310} :answer-field/id #uuid "70354c98-f319-582a-83ff-19758bae87e9" :answer-field/key "$V={\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470267} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5a9e39c-cf8a-532c-8d40-ac1ef810c40c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469312} {:answer/id #uuid "7ff70d68-31cf-5e99-9978-28a69b4ad0a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469313}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186469313} :answer-field/id #uuid "31ee54a9-4b1b-5582-ab2f-d95c19306c24" :answer-field/key "$W={\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470268}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3593d781-0056-56f1-8b48-1ee74f8fd0fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-83719" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are orthogonal?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of the given sets as \n${{u}_{1},{u}_{2},{u}_{3}},$ \n${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}},$ and \n${{w}_{1},{w}_{2}},$ respectively. \n\nThe sets $U,V,$ and $W$ are orthogonal if the following conditions on each set hold:\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle {u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0,\\,{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{3}=0,\\,{u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{3}=0.\n$$\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle {v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2}=0,\\,{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{3}=0,\\,{v}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{3}=0.\n$$\n\n- ${w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2}=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- For the set $U,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=-1+0+1=0 & ✓ \\\\ {u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{3} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=0+0+0=0 & ✓ \\\\ {u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{3} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=0+0+0=0 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the set $U$ is orthogonal.\n\n- For the set $V,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}=12+0+1=13\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $V$ is not an orthogonal set.\n\n- For the set $W,$ notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}=-40+40=0 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the set $W$ is orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"$U$ and $W$ only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351542 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca53a596-697d-5074-8ae7-cadb576b9f33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469314} {:answer/id #uuid "9028cf1d-3482-555c-9254-f303dd967e7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469315}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186469315} :answer-field/id #uuid "52cd5a79-76c1-53fd-98ef-78fe65d3a648" :answer-field/key "$U={\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470269} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a455406-0fed-5b3e-86c0-bc18ad51b9f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469316} {:answer/id #uuid "9e86cc99-94e1-57ad-bf00-0827b339489c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469317}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186469316} :answer-field/id #uuid "80e1d8bc-8a01-5f07-a31e-e1514db3104e" :answer-field/key "$V={\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470270} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45a09ee1-e29a-5fb9-b33d-83923959cc1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469318} {:answer/id #uuid "a77d1b68-ce1e-502a-b145-e7f6e0d90c36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469319}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186469319} :answer-field/id #uuid "2991993f-85de-54a4-8a97-c77e6abc7b72" :answer-field/key "$W={\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470271}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "757ea74d-034b-5cf5-b116-1f66ebbe72c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-83745" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are orthonormal?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of the given sets as \n${{u}_{1},{u}_{2}},$ \n${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}},$ and \n${{w}_{1},{w}_{2}},$ respectively. \n\nThe sets $U,V,$ and $W$ are orthonormal if the following conditions on each set hold:\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle {u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0\\,\\text{and}\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{1} &=1 \\\\ {u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{2} &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle \\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2} &=0 \\\\ {v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{3} &=0 \\\\ {v}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{3} &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\text{and}\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1} &=1 \\\\ {v}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2} &=1 \\\\ {v}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{3} &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle {w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2}=0\\,\\text{and}\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{1} &=1 \\\\ {w}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{2} &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- For the set $U,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}=-\\frac{6}{13}+\\frac{6}{13}=0 & ✓ \\\\ {u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{1} & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{4}{13}+\\frac{9}{13}=1 & ✓ \\\\ {u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{9}{13}+\\frac{4}{13}=1 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the set $U$ is orthonormal.\n\n- For the set $V,$ notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}=0+1+8=9\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $V$ is not an orthonormal set.\n\n- For the set $W,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{2}{5}-\\frac{2}{5}=0 & ✓ \\\\ {w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{1} & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{4}{5}+\\frac{1}{5}=1 & ✓ \\\\ {w}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{4}{5}=1 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $W$ is an orthonormal set.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"$U$ and $W$ only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351544 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45566415-2aae-57f0-97a6-9181c1dc7259" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349077} {:answer/id #uuid "4c12716a-e3d0-58ea-9bc6-a846ef39acb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349142} {:answer/id #uuid "6cc353d8-c713-5e4d-a946-7097098174ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349450} {:answer/id #uuid "729fa524-1af8-5a66-9373-2197ad62e564" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349501} {:answer/id #uuid "bb154ed7-8ace-5bc0-8739-903ce3a493bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350109}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186349450} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5aa3fc2-4d1c-579c-a742-d9fc0ab7d245" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351020}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1f84d773-61b5-5fc4-883c-533c2138b33d" :question/math-academy-id "q-83747" :question/problem "Consider the orthogonal set $U$ below. By adding a new vector $x=[{x}_{1},\\,{x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3}]^{T},$ extend the set so that it forms an orthogonal basis of ${R}^{3}.$ What is the value of $\\frac{{x}_{3}}{{x}_{2}}?$\n\n$$\nU={\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $U$ as ${u}_{1},\\,{u}_{2}.$ To extend the given set to an orthogonal basis of ${R}^{3}$, we need to find a third vector $x=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}$ such that\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot x &=0 \\\\ {u}_{2}\\cdot x &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system above and reduce it to its row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -9 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are two pivot columns ($1$st and $2$nd). Thus, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-3{x}_{3}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2(-3{x}_{3})+4{x}_{3}=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2{x}_{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{3} \\\\ -3{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{3}=1$, we obtain the vector \n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, an orthogonal basis of ${R}^{3}$ is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{{x}_{3}}{{x}_{2}}=\\frac{1}{-3}=-\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351545 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cd2983d-e86d-5261-9ffd-52e54967a0a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348698} {:answer/id #uuid "73c84a1a-c5d9-52a9-984a-69f99922bf98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349510} {:answer/id #uuid "acf3a4aa-5523-5a90-bfb4-0af9b5a44c38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349980} {:answer/id #uuid "c1a69118-42a6-5b62-b484-3eb05bfb2197" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350164} {:answer/id #uuid "f3e6d4b8-cac6-5ec9-86f4-03144272c6e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350582}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186350164} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fbda9ca-f49c-5215-9c1d-8f74f755ea48" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350952}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2e8b508c-7ac0-57c0-b2b3-0c7f9ae30c59" :question/math-academy-id "q-83749" :question/problem "Consider the orthogonal set $U$ below. By adding a new vector $x=[{x}_{1},\\,{x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3},\\,{x}_{4}]^{T},$ extend the set so that it forms an orthogonal basis of ${R}^{4}.$ What is the value of $\\frac{{x}_{1}}{{x}_{4}}?$\n\n$$\nU={\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $U$ as ${u}_{1},\\,{u}_{2},\\,{u}_{3}.$ To extend the given set to an orthogonal basis of ${R}^{4}$, we need to find a fourth vector $x$ such that\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot x &=0 \\\\ {u}_{2}\\cdot x &=0 \\\\ {u}_{3}\\cdot x &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1}+2{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}+2{x}_{4} &=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}+3{x}_{4} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system above and reduce it to its row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}-2 & 0 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 & 3 & 0\\end{array}\\right] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+\\frac{3}{2}{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}-2 & 0 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & 3 & 0\\end{array}\\right] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}-2 & 0 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 2 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are three pivot columns ($1$st, $2$nd and $3$rd). Thus, ${x}_{4}$ is a free variable. From the third and first equation, we get ${x}_{3}=-\\frac{1}{3}{x}_{4}$ and ${x}_{1}={x}_{3}=-\\frac{1}{3}{x}_{4}$, respectively. Substituting this into the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2}-4(-\\frac{1}{3}{x}_{4})+2{x}_{4}=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-\\frac{5}{3}{x}_{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{3}{x}_{4} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{3}{x}_{4} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}{x}_{4} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{4}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{4}=3$, we obtain the vector \n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, an orthogonal basis of ${R}^{4}$ is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, $$\n\\displaystyle \\,\\frac{{x}_{1}}{{x}_{4}}=\\frac{-1}{3}=-\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351549 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d6455e8-1d20-59ba-a6d8-2d97ffa6d4f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{30}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349002} {:answer/id #uuid "65a7868f-73dc-5fa0-a3da-94eef5365b71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{30}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349375} {:answer/id #uuid "68d65105-0045-5970-aa92-ab673f74ab63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{30}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349411} {:answer/id #uuid "cd9db71f-9801-56d4-bc24-349f1f6eb658" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{30}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350255} {:answer/id #uuid "ff44a082-cd21-564c-a383-3fa053560fc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{30}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350695}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186350695} :answer-field/id #uuid "9947e5af-d918-5be3-a9ed-34861fe2a80c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350969}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "65457e0c-9d26-538a-8f4e-c66a1a79d0d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-83763" :question/problem "Consider the **orthonormal** set $U$ below. By adding a new vector $x=[{x}_{1},\\,{x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3}]^{T},$ extend the set so that it forms an **orthonormal** basis of ${R}^{3}.$ What is the value of $|{x}_{1}|+|{x}_{2}|+|{x}_{3}|?$\n\n$$\nU={\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}}\\end{bmatrix}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $U$ as ${u}_{1},\\,{u}_{2}.$ To extend the given set to an orthonormal basis of ${R}^{3}$, we need to find a third vector $x$ such that $‖x‖=1,$ and\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot x &=0 \\\\ {u}_{2}\\cdot x &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}{x}_{1}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}{x}_{1}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}{x}_{2}+\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}}{x}_{3} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system above and reduce it to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} & 0\\end{array}\\right] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:=\\sqrt{5}\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{2}:=\\sqrt{6}\\cdot {R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2 & 0\\end{array}\\right] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{5}{2} & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are two pivot columns ($1$st and $2$nd). Thus, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-\\frac{5}{2}{x}_{3},$ and from the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{3}.$\n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{3} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{2}{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{3}=2,$ we obtain the vector \n$$\n\\displaystyle x=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$ \n\nNow, we need to normalize $x.$ Notice that $‖x‖=\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-5)^{2}+{2}^{2}}=\\sqrt{30}.$ So, we normalize $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{‖x‖}=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{30}} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{30}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{30}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, an orthonormal basis of ${R}^{3}$ is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}}\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{30}} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{30}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{30}}\\end{bmatrix}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, $$\n\\displaystyle |{x}_{1}|+|{x}_{2}|+|{x}_{3}|=|-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{30}}|+|-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{30}}|+|\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{30}}|=\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{30}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360505 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "148e1662-35f6-5380-bc45-570bd123aa65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition and scalar multiplication of matrices do not satisfy the distributive laws" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357930} {:answer/id #uuid "320b5d11-4a8f-55fe-bba8-195d9e922e5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition of matrices is not commutative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358197} {:answer/id #uuid "48109943-1239-5a7c-af98-06bb37c313df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the $2\\times 1$  zero matrix does not belong to $K$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358370} {:answer/id #uuid "7d249c29-f44d-5240-8308-3b4e8b179337" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition of matrices is not associative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358839} {:answer/id #uuid "db7e8f9f-3fef-596d-bd51-f3eb1ae8d92d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1\\cdot A\\ne A$ for all $A\\in K$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359674}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186358370} :answer-field/id #uuid "115fee41-7a55-5085-8c7d-272bb27890fe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360027}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ec097acf-f56e-507d-aaff-ec7126bba2f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-94807" :question/problem "Let $K$ be the set of all $2\\times 1$ matrices $\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},$ such that $x,y\\in R$ and $x+y=1.$  Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$K$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to matrix addition and scalar multiplication) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$K$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to matrix addition and scalar multiplication) because **the $2\\times 1$  zero matrix does not belong to $K.$***   \n\nIndeed, adding the entries of the $2\\times 1$  zero matrix yields $0+0=0\\ne 1.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- addition of matrices is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- addition and scalar multiplication of matrices  satisfy the distributive laws. $✓$\n\n- Addition of matrices  is commutative. $\\,✓$\n\n- $1\\cdot A=A$ for all $A\\in K.$ $\\,✓$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360506 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "148894ae-706f-525b-ad2d-7167fcbda468" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Addition and scalar multiplication in $J$ satisfy the distributive laws" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357929} {:answer/id #uuid "95f0bfc7-e912-5610-98e7-3d03e26ff10b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition  in $J$ is commutative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359065} {:answer/id #uuid "c0fac0ce-e1f5-5398-b1b7-b7ac03043f45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$J$ does not contain the element $-z$ for every $z\\in J$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359445} {:answer/id #uuid "c2fe1931-eb10-5327-9f81-05036c660521" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition in $J$ is associative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359465} {:answer/id #uuid "e90d5478-69f0-5aa2-9616-e0e2d300c8f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplication of $z\\in J$ by real  scalars is not closed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359820}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186359820} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb22de98-4732-5828-b969-3b30335798f8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360321}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1f59dac0-6b4c-534f-a144-e2ffbf4408ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-94809" :question/problem "Let $J$ be the set of purely imaginary complex numbers, that is, complex numbers of the form  $ai,$ where  $a$ is a nonzero real number. Complete the following sentence: \n\n*$J$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to addition of complex numbers and scalar multiplication of a complex number by a real number) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$J$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to addition of complex numbers and scalar multiplication of a complex number by a real number) because **multiplication of $z\\in J$ by real scalars is not closed.*** \n\nFor example, if $\\alpha =0$ and $z=i,$ then $\\alpha \\cdot z=0\\cdot i=0\\notin J.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- Addition in $J$ is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition  in $J$ is commutative.  $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication in $J$ satisfy the distributive laws. $\\,✓$\n\n- If  $z\\in J$ then $z=ai$ for some $a\\in R.$ Hence, $-z=(-a)i\\in J$   since $-a\\in R.$ $\\,✓$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360532 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ac32f8f-35ab-5a76-a2a3-0bf7ed6d6e5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{A2},\\text{A3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358140} {:answer/id #uuid "b02a4078-4285-53b5-8208-adf373f161e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{A1},\\text{A3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359282} {:answer/id #uuid "cebb4688-e816-564e-b206-ca5687da26d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{A1},\\text{A4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359568} {:answer/id #uuid "e1def5be-87bb-559b-8be2-e6ae570f643d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{A3},\\text{A4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359747} {:answer/id #uuid "ed42efdc-fdf0-553d-a098-acbe7e12525d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{A2},\\text{A4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359863}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186359568} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb2564e1-4315-56a6-909c-7738aa65b6ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360441}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "947236b0-fb64-5ba6-b188-fe0713019a58" :question/math-academy-id "q-94937" :question/problem "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement:*\n\n*Given any $x\\in V$, if $w$ is a vector such that $x+w=0$, then $w=-x$* \n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+w & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (x+w)+(-x) & =0+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (w+x)+(-x) & =(-x)+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,] \\\\ (w+x)+(-x) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,] \\\\ w+(x+(-x)) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A2}\\,\\,] \\\\ w+0 & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,] \\\\ w & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the vector space axioms, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+w & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (x+w)+(-x) & =0+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (w+x)+(-x) & =(-x)+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }A1\\,] \\\\ (w+x)+(-x) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,] \\\\ w+(x+(-x)) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A2}\\,\\,] \\\\ w+0 & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }A4\\,] \\\\ w & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A3}\\,\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364351 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94684f50-85e0-5b16-9c76-e95d6f808b63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364353} {:answer/id #uuid "8d44af52-39c0-527a-88ac-1519f75188fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364354} {:answer/id #uuid "bf0c3a86-73bf-5d01-8251-12828d9e1549" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364355} {:answer/id #uuid "d3bb01ba-40c0-5f98-b056-df025d672b26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364356} {:answer/id #uuid "f6a2b666-c962-5379-b707-fb1c31bee037" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364357}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364353} :answer-field/id #uuid "017cd05d-71b2-5588-bbdd-a05d4d8d7193" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364352}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6ddc2331-5b16-5155-80a8-cc824617edac" :question/math-academy-id "q-73938" :question/problem "If $r=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$ and $s=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$, then $r\\cdot s=$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the dot product, we add up the products of corresponding components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot s & ={r}_{1}\\cdot {s}_{1}+{r}_{2}\\cdot {s}_{2}+{r}_{3}\\cdot {s}_{3}+{r}_{4}\\cdot {s}_{4}+{r}_{5}\\cdot {s}_{5} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 3+(-1)\\cdot (-4)+3\\cdot 1+5\\cdot 1+2\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =3+4+3+5-4 \\\\  & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366822 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed3bb668-f155-56de-a8c2-70df13916dba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366824} {:answer/id #uuid "681d5b5f-27c4-5d62-9775-7fb94deda3bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366825} {:answer/id #uuid "e10bdba7-03c5-56be-8819-e59ca7b574b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366826} {:answer/id #uuid "be09c5e1-83a5-5086-9a71-cbc4be7d08d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366827} {:answer/id #uuid "3007c8a1-52ac-5f01-a749-68b0368a5129" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366828}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366828} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d91df29-0979-561d-b097-3e620fac7279" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366823}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7dda51cb-daef-5707-bf52-8de2fe15243f" :question/math-academy-id "q-105111" :question/problem "Let\n$r=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ z \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $s=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ z+1 \\\\ -9 \\\\ z \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}.$\nIf $r\\cdot s=1$, find the value of $z.$" :question/worked-solution "Starting from the equation $r\\cdot s=1,$ we compute the dot product in terms of $z$ and then solve for $z$ in the resulting equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot s & =1 \\\\ (-3)\\cdot 2+6\\cdot (z+1)+z\\cdot (-9)+4\\cdot z+1\\cdot 7 & =1 \\\\ -6+6z+6-9z+4z+7 & =1 \\\\ z & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $z=-6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368723 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ab93dc3-4cd4-5625-a278-abe3ff8401d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368725} {:answer/id #uuid "d42a997e-8076-5ed3-be1a-4634ac561d10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368726} {:answer/id #uuid "9541e2c9-cc7e-5d89-8ab9-ba54e9c7f31e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368727} {:answer/id #uuid "e0d2be0c-a462-511f-8ac9-c9021923f7f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368728} {:answer/id #uuid "861bf791-bfa2-5748-94c7-021348eeb523" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368729}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368725} :answer-field/id #uuid "7941dbb5-9cff-5850-ae3a-b63b47f0d7ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368724}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "506f42ad-7acb-53d3-bdad-57436806a4b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-73945" :question/problem "Let\n$l=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ y \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ and $m=\\begin{bmatrix}y+1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.$\nIf $l\\cdot m=0$, find the value of $y.$" :question/worked-solution "Starting from the equation $l\\cdot m=0,$ we compute the dot product in terms of $y$ and then solve for $y$ in the resulting equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}l\\cdot m & =0 \\\\ -1\\cdot (y+1)+2\\cdot (-2)+y\\cdot 2+6\\cdot 1+3\\cdot (-1) & =0 \\\\ -y-1-4+2y+6-3 & =0 \\\\ y-2 & =0 \\\\ y & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370894 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71774489-cfbf-54bd-8f90-2a0bee4d4a7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370896} {:answer/id #uuid "424428ba-e984-56dd-a585-b888435dd669" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{13}{19}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370897} {:answer/id #uuid "afab60d1-07e3-5634-8d3e-3874475f81cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370898} {:answer/id #uuid "843220f0-6e4a-5d90-a3c6-7c18b6a664c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{19}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370899} {:answer/id #uuid "82727867-c8e6-5d02-8aeb-92e6b06797e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370900}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370899} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e65092d-d4cf-5a8c-aa82-624d90e5b582" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370895}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "75f96dd3-b802-5102-880f-b4c303f55070" :question/math-academy-id "q-39477" :question/problem "Consider the orthogonal set $U$ below. By adding a new vector $x=[{x}_{1},\\,{x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3}]^{T},$ extend the set so that it forms an orthogonal basis of ${R}^{3}.$ What is the value of $\\frac{{x}_{1}}{{x}_{2}}?$\n\n$$\nU=\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $U$ as ${u}_{1},\\,{u}_{2}.$ To extend the given set to an orthogonal basis of ${R}^{3}$, we need to find a third vector $x=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}$ such that\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot x &=0 \\\\ {u}_{2}\\cdot x &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}+7{x}_{3} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system above and reduce it to its row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}5 & 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -4 & 7 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+\\left(-\\frac{3}{5}\\right){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}5 & 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{26}{5} & \\frac{38}{5} & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are two pivot columns ($1$st and $2$nd). Thus, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=\\frac{19}{13}{x}_{3}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1} & ={x}_{3}-2(\\frac{19}{13}{x}_{3}) \\\\ 5{x}_{1} & =-\\frac{25}{13}{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-\\frac{5}{13}{x}_{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{5}{13}{x}_{3} \\\\ \\frac{19}{13}{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{3}=13$ we obtain the vector \n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 19 \\\\ 13\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, an orthogonal basis of ${R}^{3}$ is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 19 \\\\ 13\\end{bmatrix}\\right\\}.\n$$\n\nFinally, $\\frac{{x}_{1}}{{x}_{2}}=-\\frac{5}{19}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371119 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da450b2e-ae11-5192-b330-ce437af32c6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371121} {:answer/id #uuid "fa9e6a42-9906-55c8-b6a9-3e88b997149f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371122} {:answer/id #uuid "d554bca7-593f-5921-86eb-2b5d48917f5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371123} {:answer/id #uuid "88e33fa9-23db-5560-9cc5-b599e7683d9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371124} {:answer/id #uuid "b844228e-8ce9-55e0-be6b-cc247323c110" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371125}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371121} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b4b19fa-e66f-544d-bae9-1782ab14f162" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371120}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1f896c29-487a-51e0-95fe-118554647621" :question/math-academy-id "q-81116" :question/problem "Consider the **orthonormal** set $U$ below. By adding a new vector $x=[{x}_{1},\\,{x}_{2}]^{T},$ extend the set so that it forms an **orthonormal** basis of ${R}^{2}.$ What is the value of $|{x}_{1}|+|{x}_{2}|?$\n\n$$\nU={\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5}\\end{bmatrix}}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vector of $U$ as ${u}_{1}.$ To extend the given set to an orthonormal basis of ${R}^{2}$, we need to find a second vector $x$ such that $‖x‖=1,$ and\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}\\cdot x=0\\,⟹\\,\\frac{3}{5}{x}_{1}+\\frac{4}{5}{x}_{2}=0.\n$$\n\nFrom the above equation, we get ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{4}{3}{x}_{2}.$\n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{4}{3}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{2}=-3,$ we obtain the vector \n$$\n\\displaystyle x=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$ \n\nNow, we need to normalize $x.$ Notice that $‖x‖=\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-3)^{2}}=5.$ So, we normalize $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{‖x‖}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{5}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, an orthonormal basis of ${R}^{2}$ is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5}\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{5}\\end{bmatrix}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, $$\n\\displaystyle |{x}_{1}|+|{x}_{2}|=|\\frac{4}{5}|+|-\\frac{3}{5}|=\\frac{7}{5}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371133 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb569ebe-8c7f-5e6a-a92e-eb7e20603adf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471741} {:answer/id #uuid "4f3ce39e-3082-5dec-89d3-79f955a614e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471742}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186471742} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed866305-9bff-51ed-b978-8a6b118d7503" :answer-field/key "$U={\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472376} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7637455c-7ba8-520e-a2bc-a943f2fe5e92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471743} {:answer/id #uuid "984d0634-8bc1-5008-b0d7-0eefec53c325" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471744}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186471743} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2a124fe-6d76-57c5-982d-bd22eb239e80" :answer-field/key "$V={\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472377} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d913b269-6880-5e44-8a21-3549fec7a637" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471745} {:answer/id #uuid "cf8c3fa0-0740-5d37-9928-f2fea84c3886" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471746}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186471745} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ae04b7e-1c41-5f94-831c-919f9c3158fd" :answer-field/key "$W={\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472378}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d2ecf41d-bb8c-5910-8164-c718a9bc187a" :question/math-academy-id "q-82400" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are orthonormal?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of the given sets as \n${{u}_{1},{u}_{2}},$\n${{v}_{1},{v}_{2}},$ and \n${{w}_{1},{w}_{2}}$, respectively. \n\nThe sets $U,V,$ and $W$ are orthonormal if the following conditions on each set hold:\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle {u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0\\,\\text{and}\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{1} &=1 \\\\ {u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{2} &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle {v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2}=0\\,\\text{and}\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1} &=1 \\\\ {v}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2} &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle {w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2}=0\\,\\text{and}\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{1} &=1 \\\\ {w}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{2} &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- For the set $U,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{2}{5}-\\frac{2}{5}=0 & ✓ \\\\ {u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{1} & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{4}{5}=1 & ✓ \\\\ {u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{4}{5}+\\frac{1}{5}=1 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the set $U$ is orthonormal.\n\n- For the set $V,$ notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=0+1=1\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $V$ is not an orthonormal set.\n\n- For the set $W,$ notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $W$ is not an orthonormal set.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"$U$ only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371167 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4961df63-786c-51a4-8463-13519c248902" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471759} {:answer/id #uuid "33ed506f-7ede-5020-8911-2a99c8675512" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471760}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186471760} :answer-field/id #uuid "0793ecbd-466b-509e-bfa7-5ab8226ccfad" :answer-field/key "$U={\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472385} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43dd2c4b-4b61-541d-9371-162dfd090c01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471761} {:answer/id #uuid "560c40bb-d9c4-5ef9-a866-72abd28f950f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471762}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186471761} :answer-field/id #uuid "6811c953-cf49-5c9d-af8c-b942f1a278e4" :answer-field/key "$V={\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472386} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7fd8980b-cf00-5f00-976c-a9ccb4a08e1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471763} {:answer/id #uuid "fe7dccd1-4afa-55e3-9d69-4eabc8259762" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471764}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186471763} :answer-field/id #uuid "19fc868e-69b3-5e63-9173-8bfab894feb8" :answer-field/key "$W={\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472387}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5d55bdef-1f91-5e0a-9c79-2e4df04e0183" :question/math-academy-id "q-83739" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are orthonormal?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of the given sets as \n${{u}_{1},{u}_{2}},$\n${{v}_{1},{v}_{2}},$ and \n${{w}_{1},{w}_{2}}$, respectively. \n\nThe sets $U,V,$ and $W$ are orthonormal if the following conditions on each set hold:\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle {u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0\\,\\text{and}\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{1} &=1 \\\\ {u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{2} &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle {v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2}=0\\,\\text{and}\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1} &=1 \\\\ {v}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2} &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle {w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2}=0\\,\\text{and}\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{1} &=1 \\\\ {w}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{2} &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- For the set $U,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{3}{10}-\\frac{3}{10}=0 & ✓ \\\\ {u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{1} & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{9}{10}+\\frac{1}{10}=1 & ✓ \\\\ {u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{1}{10}+\\frac{9}{10}=1 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the set $U$ is orthonormal.\n\n- For the set $V,$ notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}=-1-1=-2\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $V$ is not an orthonormal set.\n\n- For the set $W,$ notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}=-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}}\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $W$ is not an orthonormal set.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"$U$ only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382854 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37f895bf-32a0-582a-8d97-d103675f97d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A4}$, $\\text{A2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382856} {:answer/id #uuid "1424205e-d67d-53ee-af7a-6ddb217cbfbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A4}$, $\\text{A3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382857} {:answer/id #uuid "46cd3b22-e386-5fa6-aabd-63ef9e1e4cef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A2}$, $\\text{A3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382858} {:answer/id #uuid "d28fa3e4-82e9-57ec-9bf4-a7fe05ccb798" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 