& =v+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A4}\\,] \\\\ u & =v &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385324 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1337dd4f-9280-53a2-a0bf-10fa5a1172ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A4}$, $\\text{A1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385326} {:answer/id #uuid "d3b06213-6b70-5fb1-9074-bd29c49e8d32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A4}$, $\\text{A2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385327} {:answer/id #uuid "175edfb7-a947-56df-a366-83319bf965d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A2}$, $\\text{A3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385328} {:answer/id #uuid "fb4ae0dc-f023-5eac-8d6f-6539fcd8b68a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A5}$, $\\text{A2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385329} {:answer/id #uuid "f383b979-fa8e-5c2b-8977-e24abfd545ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A1}$, $\\text{A2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385330}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385328} :answer-field/id #uuid "6de75fa4-40ed-54ed-9a38-aaf2ba31ee58" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385325}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c7e8b0d2-1b58-5e69-8702-c53196883e47" :question/math-academy-id "q-35627" :question/problem "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Given any $x\\in V$, if $w$ is a vector such that $x+w=0$, then $w=-x$* \n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+w & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (x+w)+(-x) & =0+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (w+x)+(-x) & =(-x)+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A1}\\,] \\\\ (w+x)+(-x) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,] \\\\ w+(x+(-x)) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ w+0 & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ w & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the vector space axioms, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+w & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (x+w)+(-x) & =0+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (w+x)+(-x) & =(-x)+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A1}\\,] \\\\ (w+x)+(-x) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,] \\\\ w+(x+(-x)) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A2}\\,\\,] \\\\ w+0 & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ w & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A3}\\,\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385831 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1a276ce-4807-5595-9e74-b4e01dcf3dbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition in $Y$ is not associative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385833} {:answer/id #uuid "3910c94e-c1f6-54fb-9ca1-a7cfaec57a1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplication of $(x,y)\\in Y$ by a scalar is not closed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385834} {:answer/id #uuid "7f241a5e-8166-53bb-b6ac-146d6e0797cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Y$ does not contain the zero element" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385835} {:answer/id #uuid "19ee9131-fd45-5cda-a995-429bb87fe4a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition and scalar multiplication in $Y$  do not satisfy the distributive laws" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385836} {:answer/id #uuid "c7ee2446-901d-5280-8a07-74ae51b172c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition in $Y$ is not commutative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385837}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385834} :answer-field/id #uuid "a767cfd0-5f8e-59db-8dfc-c580d16b2f17" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385832}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "96e3d27f-a6f3-58f8-a748-ec53b79d0713" :question/math-academy-id "q-94808" :question/problem "Let $Y$ be the set of all ordered pairs $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$  such that $x+y\\le 3.$ Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$Y$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to the usual component-wise addition and scalar multiplication in ${R}^{2}$) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$Y$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to the usual component-wise addition and scalar multiplication in ${R}^{2}$) because **multiplication of $(x,y)\\in Y$ by a scalar is not closed.***   \n\nFor example, $(1,1)\\in Y$ because $1+1=2\\le 3.$ However, if we add the components of $2\\cdot (1,1)=(2,2),$ we get $2+2=4>3.$ So, $2\\cdot (1,1)\\notin Y.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- Addition in $Y$ is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- The zero element in $Y$ is $(0,0).$ $✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication in $Y$ satisfy the distributive laws. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition in $Y$ is commutative. $\\,✓$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386120 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5107457c-138b-51a7-92ae-a6758039472a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}16 \\\\ 24 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386122} {:answer/id #uuid "ff169898-02e2-5209-864c-d14da00b29d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}18 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386123} {:answer/id #uuid "532d0a4e-4a89-57b6-99e6-afc159ce6d1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}18 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386124} {:answer/id #uuid "87d8f2f7-2901-5f83-8b3e-f48100e7a7d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386125} {:answer/id #uuid "655d0d3d-495e-5ce2-a46b-ad3d1938e299" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386126}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386124} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c9fbf95-eeae-5173-ac51-079d67124b2a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386121}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e3e014c9-7e0f-5613-9d77-d53b9ab4992b" :question/math-academy-id "q-105102" :question/problem "Let $v=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and $w=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find $4v+2w.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply each component of $v$ by $4$ and each component of $w$ by $2.$ Then, we add the vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4v+2w & =4\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+2\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}20 \\\\ -12 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 18 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}20+(-2) \\\\ -12+18 \\\\ 8+(-4) \\\\ -4+6 \\\\ 0+(-2)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}18 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
